        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Tweak LCP render time wording]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41019</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41019"/>
        <updated>2025-09-11T09:00:03.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10931297?u=600cfcb4c4e709dfbc66b328147d846ee87b1e51&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/>

<h3 dir="auto">Description</h3>

<p dir="auto">I noticed some inaccuracies in the LCP render time page:</p>
<ul dir="auto">
<li>The top of the page states 0 will be returned for cross-origin requests but this is not the case now.</li>
<li>Therefore you cannot use a non-zero render time as a measure whether the LCP is accurate.</li>
<li>Reword the <code class="notranslate">startTime</code> section as I found that difficult to understand.</li>
</ul>
<p dir="auto">I changed this in <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="2802557127" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/37743" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/pull/37743/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/37743">#37743</a> but missed these.</p>
<h3 dir="auto">Motivation</h3>

<p dir="auto">Correct inaccuracies to avoid confusion</p>
